    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hi professor. i am studying phonetics and i'm a bit confused. can u explain the difference between voiced and unvoiced alveolar fricatives? like the difference between the /z/ and /s/ sounds? specifically how the vocal cords work here?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Hi! Alveolar fricatives, like /z/ and /s/, differ primarily in the vibration of the vocal cords. For /z/ (as in \"zeal\"), the vocal cords vibrate, producing a voiced sound. In contrast, for /s/ (as in \"see\"), the vocal cords do not vibrate, resulting in an unvoiced sound. The other factors involve the shape and position of your tongue and teeth to affect the air flow for both sounds. Practice speaking both sounds to get the feel for the difference. Good luck with your exam!",
